  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 1236 AM MDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nThe high pressure system that has been set-up over Colorado for the \nlast few days continues to propagate to the east and once it is far \nenough east southern Colorado will experience the impacts of the \nmonsoonal plume, which should start on Wednesday and will \npersist longer than the forecast period. The main impacts for \nthe forecast period will be widespread thunderstorms leading to \nflash flooding over the burn scars, urban areas, and areas with \nsaturated soils. Gusty outflow winds are expected with the \nstrongest gusts ranging from 30 to 40 MPH. While temperatures \nwill still be above average for this time of year, they are 5F \nlower than previous days this week. To keep it simple, be aware \nof Flash Flood Watches and Flash Flood Warnings, especially \nThursday and Friday when the monsoon plume is strongest.",
